Fixed3D

PROVENANCE
  Fixed3D is a fixed-point conversion of Box3D by Erin Catto
  (https://github.com/erincatto/box3d), licensed under the MIT License. Box3D's
  copyright and the MIT License (see LICENSE) are retained and apply throughout.

  The fixed-point conversion -- replacing float with Q48.16 `b3Fixed` across the engine,
  the deterministic integer transcendentals, and the supporting work -- is by
  Más Bandwidth LLC.

VENDORED LIBRARY
  The fixed-point core (the `b3Fixed` type, arithmetic, and the deterministic
  transcendentals b3Atan2 / b3ComputeCosSin) is maintained as a standalone library in
  extern/fixed (the `fixed` library) and consumed from there: box3d/fixed.h is a shim
  including "fixed/fixed.h", and the transcendentals compile from
  extern/fixed/src/fixed_math.c. See extern/fixed/NOTICE.

CREDIT
  Box3D, and the physics design this builds on, are the work of Erin Catto. Fixed3D would
  not exist without it, and useful findings are fed back upstream (see ERIN.md).

